		{
			"id": "114914310709979470",
			"parentId": "114914220548248533",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ardouglass/114914310681276071",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andrew Douglass",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ardouglass",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/359/929/909/083/745/original/c4f67e7815b7a4b6.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-25T14:20:26.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I saw the temporal polyfills as things to check out. Do you have a quick answer as to why you didn’t use one of those if Temporal compatibility is the end goal?</p><p>For context where my mind is at, my date fields are Temporal ZonedDateTime strings so I’m currently making use of addDateParsing.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114914368752703171",
			"parentId": "114914310709979470",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/114914368752703171",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-25T14:35:13.049Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ardouglass\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>ardouglass</span></a></span> I think if I started the process over again with what I know now I probably would have used one of those! I would probably even recommend other folks use those instead too.</p><p>Even more so when tree shaking lands in that smaller polyfill too: <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/temporal-polyfill#tree-shakable-api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">npmjs.com/package/temporal-pol</span><span class=\"invisible\">yfill#tree-shakable-api</span></a></p><p>At the start I wanted more ISO8601 compat (you can see that in parse-date-strings@1) but realized more strict parsing/breaking changes now was preferable to the same breaking changes later (parse-date-strings@2)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
